  "_comment": "Multidimensional structured-scene schema for the London Literary Club case, Winter 1935. The Aldgate Club, Bloomsbury. A literary executor (Charles Pemberton) dies of cardiac arrest after the evening port; the surface motive is manuscript-attribution fraud (a posthumous Marsh novel actually written by Agnes Vail née Rutherford), the buried motive is a 1921 financial scandal whose disclosure Agnes cannot allow. Carey, a rival estate solicitor, is the false plateau — placed near the corridor, motive on paper, but no access to the port. The seven minutes Wills the porter remembers is the break-token. Universal core dimensions shared with amber_cipher / attended_hour / venetian_mirror; case-specific extension SIGNATURE_TELL covers handwriting / typescript / dedication-page observables, which are central to the case's authorship pivot. Tokens listed in anchor_tokens are graph/convergence anchors only — never emitted directly.",

